[305.948006, "o", "                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              VERIFIER · HUMAN  \r\nR1  CODE-READ (declared REPRODUCED)  high      src/flask/sessions.py:96   NullSession blocks __setitem__/__delitem__/clear/pop/popitem/update/setdefault but not the `|=` operator, so `session |= {...}` on an app with no SECRET_KEY silently mutates the null session instead of raising the 'no secret key' RuntimeError, and the write is then discarded because null sessions are never saved.                         stands (codex)    \r\nR2  CODE-READ (declared REPRODUCED)  medium"]
[305.948047, "o", "    src/flask/sessions.py:334  open_session catches only BadSignature, but itsdangerous raises BadPayload (a sibling of BadSignature under BadData) when a correctly-signed cookie's payload cannot be deserialized, so such a cookie propagates an exception out of open_session and 500s every request instead of degrading to an empty session.                                stands (codex)    \r\nR3  "]
[305.94809, "o", "CODE-READ                        low       src/flask/sessions.py:330  open_session applies max_age=PERMANENT_SESSION_LIFETIME to every cookie including non-permanent ones, whose cookie carries no Expires and whose timestamp is only refreshed when the session is modified, so a long-lived non-permanent browser session is server-side rejected after the lifetime while the browser keeps sending it.             stands (codex)    \r\n"]
[305.948124, "o", "R4  CODE-READ                        low       src/flask/sessions.py:30   The `permanent` property is annotated `-> bool` and its setter coerces with bool(), but the getter returns app.get(\"_permanent\", False) uncoerced, so a session that got \"_permanent\" set through a non-property path returns a non-bool from a bool-typed property.                                                        "]
[305.948151, "o", "                       stands (codex)    \r\nR5  HYPOTHESIS"]
[305.948178, "o", "                       low       src/flask/sessions.py:373  save_session dereferences get_signing_serializer(app) with a `# type: ignore[union-attr]` and no None guard, so if app.secret_key becomes falsy between open_session and save_session, or a subclass reaches save_session without the null-session gate, the failure is an opaque AttributeError on None rather than the 'no secret key' message.  "]
